use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Dragging import Dragging
from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation

export ui-component Slider:
    description:
        A slider sets a number by dragging a handle along a track, between a
        minimum and a maximum, like a volume control. It has one handle for a
        single number, or two for a range such as a price from $10 to $50. It
        moves smoothly or in fixed steps.

    behaviors:
        - @{Dragging}
        - @{FormParticipation}

    pointer:
        The user drags a handle to change the value. Clicking or tapping the
        track moves the nearest handle to that spot.

    keyboard:
        Each handle can be focused on its own. The arrow keys move it by one
        step, Page Up and Page Down by a bigger step, and Home and End to the
        minimum and maximum.

    range:
        With two handles, they can't pass each other. Each handle can only go
        as far as the other one. The component can also keep a minimum gap
        between them, such as at least $5. Whether a slider can have more than
        two handles is up to the chosen library.

    fill:
        The part of the track between the minimum and the handle is filled in.
        The component can instead fill from another point, such as the middle
        of a slider running from -50 to 50. With two handles, the part between
        them is filled.

    reporting:
        The component is told about changes continuously while a handle moves,
        and again once when the user lets go, so it can choose to act only on
        the final value.

    valueText:
        Assistive tools read out the value, which can be friendlier text than
        the raw number, such as "$50" or "Medium".

    direction:
        A slider can run across or up and down. One running across is
        reversed for right-to-left languages.

    disabled:
        A disabled slider can't be moved or focused, and it's clear to the user
        that it's unavailable. A read-only slider can be focused and read out,
        but not moved.

    marks:
        Whether it shows marks along the track, or the value while dragging,
        is up to the chosen library.

    nonGoals:
        - Not for entering an exact number. Pair it with a NumberInput if that
            matters
